    "multicolumn_jJeRJz": {
      "type": "multicolumn",
      "blocks": {
        "column_with_icon_byhYEV": {
          "type": "column_with_icon",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "icon_size": 64,
            "title": "",
            "text": "<p>Most teams work hard on acquisition, activation, and onboarding, but still struggle with the real test of product value:</p><ul><li>Why do users drop off after trying the product?</li><li>Why do some products become part of a routine while others get forgotten?</li><li>Why do some experiences create momentum, mastery, and loyalty?</li><li>Why do users engage deeply with one product but only occasionally with another?</li></ul>",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_url": ""
          }
        },
        "column_with_icon_K88pdy": {
          "type": "column_with_icon",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "icon_size": 64,
            "title": "",
            "text": "<p>This book is built around those questions.</p><p>It focuses on the psychology behind engagement and habit formation, then turns that into practical product design guidance.</p>",
            "link_text": "",
            "link_url": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "column_with_icon_byhYEV",
        "column_with_icon_K88pdy"
      ],
